  "scope": "An authored visual prop becomes a world-rendered object following a spawned dynamic box at the same committed tick. The checks cover native service release, contact and same-build cold continuation.",
  "checks": [
    "Invalid template, excessive velocity, stale tick, initially overlapping box and removal of an owned proxy reject the request. A repaired request mints the expected ID and exact retry reuses it.",
    "Same-tick item matrix continuity, translated collision frame, requested velocities, independent falling and rotation, live floor contact and asleep rest.",
    "The restored release, active floor contact and settled state match whole archive bytes. Reattach with keep-world and retire the collision proxy.",
    "The observer gains two prop draws, the player loses the corresponding foreground draws, and the selected restored launch and in-flight Vulkan frames exactly match the continuous run."
  ],
